Agenda item 10 at the 13 May 2025 AGM concerns a Domination and Profit & Loss Transfer Agreement (PLTA) between Rheinmetall AG and its 100%‑owned Rheinmetall Digital GmbH (formerly RRS – MITCOS Rheinmetall Rohde & Schwarz Military IT and Communications Solutions GmbH), accompanied by a joint report under Section 293a AktG covering fiscal year 2024.
Rheinmetall Digital GmbH’s annual financial statements for years ending 31 Dec 2022, 2023 and 2024 (German only) are presented for approval of the PLTA—enabling direct consolidation of its P&L and balance sheet into the Group from FY2025 onwards.
Rheinmetall Group’s FY2024 consolidated sales rose 36% to €9,751 million, with operating result +61% to €1,478 million (margin 15.2%) and backlog €55.0 billion; the PLTA will channel RD GmbH’s results into these headline figures and could stabilize margins through recurring digital service revenues.
Under the PLTA, intra‑group receivables/payables between Rheinmetall AG and Rheinmetall Digital GmbH will be eliminated, potentially adjusting consolidated equity (via goodwill or capital consolidation) and impacting net debt ratios that stood at €9.8 billion net debt at end‑2024.
This PLTA follows a similar agreement in May 2024 between Rheinmetall AG and Rheinmetall Liegenschaften und Vermietung GmbH, indicating a strategic pattern to centralize subsidiary profits, optimize tax positions and strengthen cash flow visibility across the Group.
The joint report to shareholders will detail the balance sheet effects, including any recognition of hidden reserves or liabilities––pension, deferred taxes and contract margin adjustments––emanating from the consolidation of Rheinmetall Digital GmbH into Rheinmetall AG post‑2024.
